.TH smi-pki-do-cert-request "1" "September 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI PKI Command"
.SH NAME
smi-pki-do-cert-request \- Create a server private key, public key and CSR
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-pki-do-cert-request
.I DIRECTORY DOMAIN_NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Creates the private key, public key and CSR for \fIDOMAIN_NAME\fR in \fIDIRECTORY\fR, with subjectAltName \fBDNS:DOMAIN_NAME\fR, exact host, no wildcard.
It is a thin command line wrapper over the matching function in the file based PKI library
\fBpki.sh\fR, so each step of building a CA and signing certificates can be run and inspected
on its own. All material is passed as file names; the command fails if the underlying OpenSSL
operation fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smi-pki-ca-create (1),
.BR smi-pki-create-domain-cert (1),
.BR openssl (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Imre Tabur <imre.tabur@mail.ee>
